Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:24:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PUBLISH-FIX-99: the order-book stage widens 6 -> 20 on
 measured headroom
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner: 'why can't it have 600 not six honestly why can't you build that? ... let it start with 600 and
the ones that make it through make it through.'

He is right, and the six was never the width of the funnel. The wide eye already sweeps all 612 USD
pairs and the collector streams 1-minute candles for the accepted catalog (~90 ranked per refresh).
Six was the width of the LAST chamber only — the coins whose live L2 order book is streaming, which
is required because that is what proves the protective exit at depth.

And six was chosen when the process sat at 88-91% event-loop utilisation with 78% of its busy time
inside fsync. PUBLISH-FIX-97 measured the same workload at 56-61%:
  'CPU LOAD 60s: busy 33343ms idle 26657ms (event-loop utilization 56%)' — deployment ac337e1f
So the headroom is measured, not assumed.

- universeExpansion.hotLane.slots 6 -> 20 (audited in the SCOPE-5 config fence).
- the watch offers picks 6 -> 20, band 12 -> 30.  had been sized to the JUDGE's six preparation
  slots, but the watch feeds the TAPE and the Judge prepares its best six from what the tape carries —
  tying them together meant the Judge chose six out of six. It now chooses the best six OF TWENTY,
  ordered by FIX-98 fitness.
- policy.universe.preparationSlots / maxCandidates UNCHANGED at 6. The account policy is immutable;
  no policy byte was touched and the fee080 binding stands.

The shipped-constant guards written earlier tonight (publish-fix-94 FIX94-6, publish-fix-96 FIX96-5,
learning-volatility-watch VW-04) caught this change and were updated with the reason — which is
exactly what they were written for.

Green: social-4f-scope 9, learning-volatility-watch 4, publish-fix-94 7, publish-fix-96 5,
publish-fix-98 6, tape-hot-lane 4, coin-dossier 3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
